# Auto framework paths — overwrite on every sync update
# Consumed by bin/auto-sync and the release mirror job
#
# Format: one path or glob per line, relative to the repo root.
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
#
# To add a new framework path when extending Auto:
#   1. Append a line here (path or glob, relative to repo root).
#   2. Update the Framework bucket table in docs/auto/file-buckets.md.
#   3. Run tests/test-framework-paths.sh to confirm the path resolves.
#
# Entries annotated "# (added by issue/NNN)" are not yet present in this
# repo but are reserved for future issues; the test skips them.
# Remove the annotation once the file is created so the test validates it.

